WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.049
This fictional visit was recorded in
healthctl.

2
00:00:03.049 --> 00:00:04.706
Model waits are shortened.

3
00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:08.259
In New encounter, the patient describes
something unusual.

4
00:00:08.259 --> 00:00:12.533
At choir practice, their own voice echoes
in their left ear.

5
00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:18.736
My own words first leaves room to describe
something the app hasn’t suggested.

6
00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:22.367
The app opens by asking how the symptom
has changed.

7
00:00:22.367 --> 00:00:27.515
The patient adds that humming a low note
brings on the echo, even alone in a

8
00:00:27.515 --> 00:00:28.158
quiet room.

9
00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:35.478
The connected model asks, “Apart from the
echo, has it become harder to hear

10
00:00:35.478 --> 00:00:38.879
in your left ear?” This is the question
the patient saw.

11
00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:42.724
The patient can still hear people talking.

12
00:00:42.724 --> 00:00:46.769
It’s their own voice that sounds hollow,
especially after running to

13
00:00:46.769 --> 00:00:50.078
rehearsal. They type that distinction in
their own words.

14
00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:55.104
The model asks about the beginning of the
episode.

15
00:00:55.104 --> 00:00:59.698
Did other sounds suddenly get harder to
hear around the time the echo started?

16
00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:04.139
In history review, the patient checks
their calendar.

17
00:01:04.139 --> 00:01:08.996
They change the timing to two rehearsals
ago, save the correction, and confirm

18
00:01:08.996 --> 00:01:09.743
the history.

19
00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:12.846
The clinician brief now includes the
corrected timing.

20
00:01:12.846 --> 00:01:16.889
The patient can take this history to a
qualified healthcare professional to

21
00:01:16.889 --> 00:01:17.900
verify the findings.

22
00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:21.617
The patient downloads the visit record
from the Report tab.
